before:
The supplied HTML is separate from the CSS.

```html
<div class="cards"><p>North</p><p>South</p></div>
```

```css
.cards { display: block; }
@supports (display: grid) { .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 100px 100px; } }
```

after:
These cards start as blocks. A browser that supports Grid gets two columns.
```css
.cards { display: block; }
@supports (display: grid) {
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 100px 100px;
  }
}
```
